## 3. Universal CBM recipe – Entry points & business flows

Run these steps in order. Do **not** rely only on `get_architecture`.

### Step A – Index

```bash
codebase-memory-mcp cli index_repository --repo-path /path/to/repo
codebase-memory-mcp cli list_projects          # note the exact project name
```

### Step B – High-level map

```bash
codebase-memory-mcp cli get_architecture --project PROJECT \
  --aspects '["hotspots","routes","structure","languages"]'
```

### Step C – Structural roots (functions nothing calls)

```bash
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_graph --project PROJECT \
  --label Function --max-degree 0 --limit 50
```

### Step D – Name-pattern sweeps (broad → specific)

**Universal first pass (covers most apps):**

```bash
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_graph --project PROJECT \
  --name-pattern "main|cli|app|server|start|run|handler|router|controller|entrypoint|entry_point|bootstrap|init|listen|serve|worker|consumer|process|job|task|lambda|handler" \
  --label Function --limit 60
```

**Class / type level:**

```bash
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_graph --project PROJECT \
  --name-pattern "Application|App|Server|Router|Controller|Command|Group|Worker|Consumer|Handler|Service|Job|Task" \
  --label Class --limit 40
```

### Step E – Route / HTTP / RPC entry points

```bash
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_graph --project PROJECT --label Route
```

### Step F – Process / executable entry points

```bash
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_graph --project PROJECT --label Process
```

### Step G – Text search for language idioms

```bash
# Python
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern '__name__\s*==\s*[\'"]__main__[\'"]'

# Go
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern 'func\s+main\s*\('

# Node / JS / TS
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern 'require\.main\s*===\s*module|#\!/usr/bin/env'

# Java / Kotlin
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern 'public\s+static\s+void\s+main'

# Rust
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern 'fn\s+main\s*\('

# General shebang / scripts
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern '^#!/'
```

### Step H – Expand the real business flows

```bash
codebase-memory-mcp cli trace_path --project PROJECT \
  --function-name "ExactFunctionName" \
  --direction outbound --depth 4 --limit 30
```

