## 4. Finding all functional tests

Functional tests (also called integration tests, end-to-end tests, feature tests, system tests, acceptance tests) verify behaviour through real or near-real entry points.  
Unit tests are usually more numerous; this section focuses on **functional / integration / e2e** style tests while still showing how to surface the broader test surface.

### 4.1 What CBM already knows about tests

CBM frequently creates `TESTS` edges and can surface test functions/classes.  
However, automatic classification is incomplete, so we again use a **multi-signal** approach.

### 4.2 Universal test-discovery recipe

#### A. Search by common test naming conventions

```bash
# Function / method level
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_graph --project PROJECT \
  --name-pattern "test_|_test$|Test|it_|describe_|spec_|should_|feature_|scenario_|e2e_|integration_|functional_" \
  --label Function --limit 80

# Class level (JUnit, TestNG, pytest classes, etc.)
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_graph --project PROJECT \
  --name-pattern "Test|Spec|Suite|Feature|Scenario" \
  --label Class --limit 50
```

#### B. Search by file / path patterns (very reliable)

```bash
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_graph --project PROJECT \
  --file-pattern ".*(test|tests|spec|specs|e2e|integration|functional|features|__tests__|cypress|playwright|selenium).*" \
  --limit 100
```

#### C. Text search for framework idioms

```bash
# Python (pytest, unittest, behave, robot)
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern 'def test_|@pytest\.|unittest\.|@given|@when|@then|Feature:|Scenario:'

# JavaScript / TypeScript (Jest, Vitest, Mocha, Cypress, Playwright, Testing Library)
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern 'describe\(|it\(|test\(|expect\(|cy\.|test\(|page\.|@playwright|render\('

# Java / Kotlin (JUnit, TestNG, Spock, Cucumber)
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern '@Test|@ParameterizedTest|@Given|@When|@Then|def ".*"'

# Go
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern 'func Test|t\.Run\(|testify|gomock'

# Rust
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern '#\[test\]|#\[tokio::test\]|mod tests'

# C# / .NET
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern '\[Fact\]|\[Theory\]|\[TestMethod\]|\[Test\]'

# Ruby
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_code --project PROJECT --pattern 'RSpec\.|describe |it |feature |scenario '
```

#### D. Use the TESTS relationship when present

```bash
# Functions that have TESTS edges (CBM already linked them)
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_graph --project PROJECT \
  --relationship TESTS --limit 50
```

#### E. Distinguish functional vs pure unit tests (heuristic)

| Signal | More likely **functional / integration / e2e** | More likely **unit** |
|--------|-----------------------------------------------|----------------------|
| File path | `e2e/`, `integration/`, `functional/`, `features/`, `cypress/`, `playwright/`, `selenium/` | `unit/`, `__tests__` next to source, `*_test.go` next to file |
| Name | `test_end_to_end`, `test_api_flow`, `test_user_journey`, `Feature`, `Scenario` | `test_add`, `test_parse`, `test_helper` |
| Imports / setup | Starts real server, browser, database, message broker, HTTP client to real port | Mocks, stubs, in-memory fakes only |
| Calls real entry points | Calls `main`, route handlers, agent `invoke`, CLI runner | Calls pure functions / private methods |

Practical filter after you have candidates:

```bash
# Keep only tests that live under typical functional folders
codebase-memory-mcp cli search_graph --project PROJECT \
  --file-pattern ".*(e2e|integration|functional|features|cypress|playwright|selenium|acceptance).*" \
  --name-pattern "test_|it_|describe_|spec_|feature_|scenario_" \
  --limit 60
```

### 4.3 Linking tests back to entry points & business flows

Once you have both entry points and tests:

```bash
# From a known entry point, see what tests cover it (if TESTS edges exist)
codebase-memory-mcp cli trace_path --project PROJECT \
  --function-name "YourEntryPoint" --direction inbound --depth 2

# Or the other way: from a test, see what it exercises
codebase-memory-mcp cli trace_path --project PROJECT \
  --function-name "test_user_registration_flow" --direction outbound --depth 4
```

This is the fastest way to answer:

- “Which functional tests exercise this API / agent / page?”
- “Which business flows have no functional coverage?”

### 4.4 App-type notes for tests

| App kind              | Typical functional-test locations / frameworks                      | Extra patterns |
|-----------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------|
| **API / backend**     | `tests/integration`, `tests/e2e`, `*_test.go`, Testcontainers       | `TestClient`, `APITestCase`, `supertest`, `rest-assured` |
| **Frontend**          | Cypress, Playwright, Testing Library, Jest + MSW                    | `cy.`, `page.`, `render(`, `screen.` |
| **Agentic**           | Often custom; look for `test_agent`, `test_graph`, `test_tool`      | `invoke`, `ainvoke`, `stream`, mock LLM responses |
| **CLI**               | CliRunner (Click), `go test`, snapshot tests                        | `CliRunner`, `runner.invoke` |
| **Mobile**            | Detox, Espresso, XCUITest, Flutter integration_test                 | `integration_test`, `espresso`, `XCUITest` |
| **Monolith**          | Usually has both unit + a smaller set of integration/e2e suites     | Look under `tests/integration` + `tests/e2e` |
| **Serverless**        | Local emulators + integration tests against deployed stages         | `serverless-offline`, `sam local`, `test_handler` |

