## 8. How `name-pattern` works

`--name-pattern` is a **regex** matched against the **symbol name** (function/method/class name), not the full file path.

Useful examples:

```bash
# Single word
--name-pattern "main"

# Alternation (OR)
--name-pattern "main|cli|app|handler|run|start"

# Test-oriented
--name-pattern "test_|it_|describe_|spec_|feature_"

# Starts with
--name-pattern "^handle"

# Combined with label
--name-pattern "main|cli" --label Function
--name-pattern "Test|Spec" --label Class
```

You do **not** need every possible word. Use short lists of common entry-style and test-style words and run 2–4 targeted searches.

